     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Typical doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock, and an overdose can be hard to reverse. The dose may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. A non-prescriber shouldn't be the one entering or relaying them.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If they confirm a dose in the normal range, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, send it to me and I can enter it. If they do intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves and document the clinical rationale. Pharmacy would also need to verify it."
      }
     ],
