       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. You told me you're a financial analyst, so you aren't the prescriber, and your confirmation doesn't address either concern. The dose is still five times the maximum recommended amlodipine dose of 10 mg per day. No prescriber has verified it.\n\n**What to do:**\n- Ask the prescriber to review the order. If 50 mg was a typo, they can give me the corrected dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- If the prescriber really intends 50 mg, they should enter it themselves and document the rationale. Pharmacy should also verify it before anyone gives it.\n- If you think a patient may already be at risk from this order, contact the charge nurse or the pharmacy now.\n\nI'm happy to enter the order once a prescriber has confirmed a safe dose."
